_refine_special_details          
;
The crystal was determined to be a inversion twin based on the value of the Flack parameter. Refinement as an inversion twin gave a BASF value of 0.45(3).
Thermal parameters were refined anisotropically for all non-hydrogen atoms.  
Hydrogen atoms were placed in ideal positions and refined using a riding model.
Co(F-bdp) is a flexible metal-organic framework which maintains an open structure containing solvent molecules in the as-synthesized form.
However, the diethylformamide (DEF) solvent molecules in the framework pores were severely disordered and could not be modeled.  
Consequently, the unassigned electron density was accounted for using SQUEEZE as implemented in the PLATON interface. Refinement before SQUEEZE was applied gave an R1 of 10.06% (wR2 = 30.99%), while applying SQUEEZE resulted in an R1 of 2.97% (wR2 = 8.44%).

The fluorobenzene rings on the organic linkers were found to be disordered. The site occupancies for fluorine substituents on the two crystallographically disticnt benzene ring positions were fixed to 25% to reflect statistical disorder over the 
four ring positions (two crystallographically distinct positions and their symmetry equivalents generated by the two-fold axis through the ring).
The site occupancies for the associated hydrogen atoms on the corresponding benzene ring positions were fixed to 75%.

Refinement of Co(F-bdp) was first attempted in the space group P4(3), which yeilded comparable R-factors. Free refinement of the disordered fluorine substituent over the 4 possible benzene ring positions in the space group P4(3) suggested a possible 
preference for three ring positions over the fourth. However, no physical reasoning could be identified for this preference. Further, the PLATON routine ADDSYM suggested that the data were more consistent with the presently assigned space group, 
P4(3)22. Therefore, in the absense of higher-resolution data, an averaged disorder in the higher-symmetry space group P4(3)22 as described above was selected as the most reasonable structural model.
;
_vrf_PLAT213_mkt004s_sq          
;
PROBLEM: Atom F2              has ADP max/min Ratio .....        4.5 prolat
RESPONSE: The  disordered fluorine atom on the fluorobenzene ring results in large values in the displacement parameters in the direction of the disorder. This causes the atomic displacement parameters
to be much larger along the direction of the disorder in comparison to those perpendicular to it.
;
_vrf_PLAT250_mkt004s_sq          
;
PROBLEM: Large U3/U1 Ratio for Average U(i,j) Tensor ....        4.7 Note  
RESPONSE: The large average U3/U1 ratio likely arises from slight disorder from rotation and flexing of the fluorobenzene ring, which causes the displacement parameters on the ring atoms to be large in the direction of disorder.
;
