_refine_special_details          
;
Diffraction data were collected at room temperature following observation of poor diffraction upon slow or flash-cooling of the crystals to 100 K. Due to the room temperature data collection, DEF molecules in the pore were highly disordered and could not be resolved. Therefore, the Platon routine SQUEEZE was used following refinement of the complete framework structure model.

All non-hydrogen atoms were refined anisotropically. Hydrogen and deuterium atoms were placed geometrically and refined using a riding model.

The structure was refined as an inversion twin with a twin fraction of 0.48(4).
;
